  {
   "t": "cardFlip",
   "in": "dolly",
   "pillar": "eat",
   "say": "The story goes that Cardinal *Richelieu* was so disgusted by a guest picking his teeth with the point of his knife that he had the tips of his own table knives ground *round*.",
   "p": {
    "frontLabel": "THE STORY GOES",
    "heard": "A guest picks his teeth with a knife point.",
    "backLabel": "SO, THE STORY GOES",
    "actual": "Richelieu had his knives ground round.",
    "source": "Wikipedia: Table knife (a tradition)",
    "flipOn": "ground"
   }
  },
  {
   "t": "exhibits",
   "in": "dolly",
   "pillar": "eat",
   "say": "And in *1669*, King Louis the Fourteenth reportedly went further, and banned pointed table knives.",
   "p": {
    "tag": "FRANCE · 1669",
    "word": "Banned.",
    "items": [
     {
      "obj": "knife",
      "meta": "FRANCE · 1669",
